  publicly.'
hypothesis: Does the epoch axis keep paying? v062 established that stacking three
  step-size levers collapses into one quantity, and v064 established that a SINGLE
  axis pushed 8x beats all three stacked. The open question is whether training length
  has saturated at 8 or still has room at 16. Costs 212,144 steps against v064's 106,072,
  so roughly double again. If 16 lands near 0.6895 the axis has saturated and 8 epochs
  was the right budget; if it lands materially higher the axis was still the binding
  constraint at 8 and was never the model's ceiling.
